{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, יַתִּיר","hw":"יַתִּיר","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">יַתִּיר</span></big>  <strong>adj. pre-eminent, surpassing (</strong>v. BH <a data-ref=\"BDB, יֶ֫תֶר\" href=\"/BDB,_יֶ֫תֶר\", dir=\"rtl\">יתר</a><strong>)</strong>;—ms. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:31\" href=\"/Daniel.2.31\">Dn 2:31</a>; fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">יַתִּירָא</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:4\" href=\"/Daniel.6.4\">6:4</a>, usually <span dir=\"rtl\">ה—ָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:33\" href=\"/Daniel.4.33\">4:33</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:12\" href=\"/Daniel.5.12\">5:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:14\" href=\"/Daniel.5.14\">14</a>; as adv. <em>exceedingly</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:22\" href=\"/Daniel.3.22\">3:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:7\" href=\"/Daniel.7.7\">7:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:19\" href=\"/Daniel.7.19\">19</a> (cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יתיר מתבריך</span> Eut<sup>Sin. 498</sup> wh. Lzb <sup>401</sup> reads <span dir=\"rtl\">יתירית בריך</span>).","next":"BDB Aramaic, כְּ","prev":"BDB Aramaic, יְתִב"}